<title>CHINA: China Chengdao oil output exceeds 1.0 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>China Chengdao oil output exceeds 1.0 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Chengdao offshore oilfield in the eastern province of Shandong produced 1.02 million tonnes of oil to December 14, an official of the oilfield said on Monday.</p>
<p>Chengdao had been forecast to produce 1.0 million tonnes in 1996, but it now expects output to hit 1.05 million tonnes, the official said by telephone. Output was 540,000 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>Chengdao is part of the Shengli oilfield, China's second largest.</p>
</text>
